 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Isosurfaces](13788-isosurfaces.md)
-An isosurface is a surface connecting points of similar properties in space, the higher-dimensional correspondent to isolines. It is a surface in 3D space that intersects voxels having a constant value, similar to a 2D isocontour. This concept underpins the geometry rendered by Multi-Isosurface Rendering.
+An isosurface is a surface connecting points of similar properties in space, the higher-dimensional correspondent to isolines. It is a surface in 3D space that intersects voxels having a constant value, similar to a 2D isocontour. This concept underpins the geometry rendered by Multi-Isosurface Rendering. It sets itself apart from volume-based methods by providing explicit polygonal geometry rather than sampled voxel data, making it the preferred choice when interactive mesh rendering or standard rasterization pipelines are required.
 
